    "pre_update_notes": "A patch release on top of 2.3.5: every page no longer answers a second time under an /index.php/ prefix (search engines had indexed such copies; they now redirect to the clean address), the company address in the home page structured data is a proper address, a very large catalogue no longer leaves a half-written sitemap when you press Regenerate sitemap now (the nightly run builds it), and importing a site onto a shop that still has visitors no longer stops on its log tables and is much faster from the command line. There is no database change; nothing in your products, orders, invoices, payments or customers is changed or removed. Update from a single browser tab and leave the update page open until it finishes.",
    "post_update_notes": "After the update: nothing needs to be done. If your catalogue is very large (hundreds of thousands of parts) the Regenerate sitemap now button tells you it will not run from the queue; the sitemap is then built every night, or run php artisan sitemap:generate on the server.",
